    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d350">

                <pb facs="0568" n="482" sameAs="frus:frus1927v01/pg482"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">701.4211/58</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The British Ambassador</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Howard</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1927-01-24"><hi rendition="#italic">January 24,
                        1927</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 49</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honour to refer to your note of
                    December 4th last,<anchor n="6" xml:id="d350-f1"/> notifying me that the
                    appointment of the Honourable Vincent Massey as His Majesty’s Envoy
                    Extraordinary and Minister Plenipotentiary to represent the interests of the
                    Dominion of Canada in the United States will be entirely agreeable to the United
                    States Government.</p>
                <p>In this connection, I have the honour to state that Mr. Massey has now advised me
                    that he proposes to arrive at Washington at the end of the second week in
                    February and is desirous of presenting his letters <pb facs="0569" n="483"
                        xml:id="pg483"/> of credence on any day between the 15th and 19th of
                    February. I should accordingly be most grateful if you would be so good as to
                    notify me at your earliest convenience on what date it will be convenient for
                    the President to receive Mr. Massey for the presentation of his credentials. At
                    the same time, I have the honour to inform you that the Government of Canada are
                    desirous that I should accompany Mr. Massey to the White House on this
                    occasion.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Esme Howard</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
